DESIGN REFERENCE DISCUSSION
------------------------------
The user shared reference mockups showing a fuller sidebar-based
dashboard style (separate nav items for Users, Roles & Permissions,
Deployments, Cost Overview, Audit Logs, etc.) for both a User and an
Admin view.

Decision made: rather than rebuilding today's dashboard to match this
immediately, we mapped each element in the reference to where it
already fits in the 35-day plan:
- Summary cards + status donut chart + request table -> already
  covered by Day 13 (today) and Day 16 (admin version)
- "New Request" / "Smart Recommendation" / "Cost Estimation" cards ->
  Day 14, Day 26, and Day 27 respectively
- Sidebar nav items like Users, Roles & Permissions, Audit Logs, Cost
  Overview as separate pages, and the "Auto Stop Policy" banner -> NOT
  part of the original 35-day scope; flagged as optional stretch goals
  only if time remains near the end, to avoid scope creep before the
  Oct/Nov deadline

Agreed plan: apply the fuller sidebar/full-width visual style
specifically on Day 16 (Admin Dashboard) and do a final polish pass on
Day 17, once real backend data (approvals, deployments) exists to
populate it - rather than building an elaborate UI now and having to
redo it later.

